{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/cor-quantum-dilogarithm","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Corollary","doco:Section"],"label":"cor:quantum-dilogarithm","kind":"corollary","title":"Quantum Dilogarithm as Localized Torsion Volume","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-topological-mass","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-briggs-klein-chart"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-quantum-dilogarithm"],"tags":["quantum-dilogarithm","torsion-volume","reeb-flow","archimedean"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Torsion.quantum_dilogarithm","text":"quantum-dilogarithm.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/quantum-dilogarithm.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"cor:quantum-dilogarithm\"></a><p>In the archimedean realisation, the transient trace contribution <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{tr}_{\\mathrm{trans}}(\\varrho, p_i)</code> from the <a href=\"#thm:topological-mass\">topological decomposition of mass</a> identically evaluates to the quantum dilogarithm <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Phi_q(z_i)</code>. Here, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z_i</code> denotes the exact spectral coordinate of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p_i</code> within the Briggs–Klein chart (<a href=\"#def:briggs-klein-chart\">Briggs–Klein chart</a>).</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/quantum-dilogarithm.md","heading":"Corollary","number":"5.13.1"}
